WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
Brackhaven.

2
00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:06.130
A small seaside town with a
harbour, a beach and a row of shops.

3
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.120
A glossy tourism page invites
you in: cobbled lanes,

4
00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:13.930
a golden beach, sunsets
you'll never forget.

5
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.140
Then a local news page describes the
same seafront after a night of trouble.

6
00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.380
Both are about one place.

7
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.580
So which one is telling the truth?

8
00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:27.250
In this mission, you'll put
both pages under the same lens,

9
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.040
detail by detail.

10
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:34.290
You'll test how word choice, naming and
grammar shape the way we see a place.

11
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.670
And you'll ask whether a news
report can ever be just the facts.

12
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.620
Your mission: decide which
description of the town is true.
